# Per-project superhuman working docs (VISION / REQUIREMENTS / DESIGN / PLAN /
# TEST / SUPERHUMAN / DECISIONS) stay LOCAL. They record a specific operator's
# environments, hosts, and internal vocabulary as a matter of course, and this
# repo is published, so they must never become tracked files. The publication
# guard in tests/test_content.py scans `git ls-files`, which means an untracked
# doc is invisible to it by construction — this rule is what keeps it that way.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash so the synthetic-bug fixture under
# tests/smoke/.../docs/superhuman/ is unaffected.
/docs/superhuman/*/
# Deliberately published, and scrubbed of operator specifics before they were:
!/docs/superhuman/specs/
